     As detailed above, the actuator of the actuator assembly is a piezoelectric disk actuator that flexes such that opposite sides of the disk move in the first direction upon application of electrical current thereto and flexes such that the opposite sides of the disk move in the second direction upon at least one of a cessation of application of the electrical current thereto or application of a current having an opposite polarity than that which was applied to flex the disk in the first direction. With respect to the former phenomenon, the piezoelectric disk  793  can have a relaxed state that is bowed in the direction of the second chamber  791 , and only deforms into the direction of the first chamber  793  upon the application of the current. With respect to the latter phenomenon, the piezoelectric disk  793  can have a relaxed state that is flat/that neither extends in the first chamber nor extends in a second chamber without the application of a current thereto—the first polarity of the current causes the piezoelectric disk to deflect into the first chamber, and the second polarity (the opposite polarity) causes the piezoelectric disk to deflect into the second chamber. 
