An apparatus configured to decode video data, the apparatus comprising:
 a memory configured to store luma blocks of one or more of a picture, a slice, a tile, or a tile group and chroma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group; and   one or more processors, implemented in circuitry and in communication with the memory, the one or more processors configured to:
 decode, from a video bitstream for which adaptive loop filtering is enabled for the luma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group, a first syntax element indicating a number of adaptive parameter sets for the luma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group; 
 decode a plurality of first adaptive parameter set indices for the luma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group based on the number of adaptive parameter sets for the luma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group; 
 decode, from the video bitstream for which adaptive loop filtering is enabled for the chroma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group, a second adaptive parameter set index for the chroma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group; 
 apply first adaptive loop filters to the luma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group based on the plurality of first adaptive parameter set indices; and 
 apply a second adaptive loop filter to the chroma blocks of the one or more of the picture, the slice, the tile, or the tile group based on the second adaptive parameter set index.

A method of managing a mobile network, the method comprising:
 an Access and Mobility Function (AMF) receiving, from an Access Network (AN), a Notification message comprising information identifying at least one PDU session to be deactivated, the information including at least one PDU Session ID with an active N3 user plane;   responsive to receipt of the Notification message, the AMF:
 sending a Release Request message to the Access Network (AN); 
 identifying each SMF associated with the at least one PDU session to be deactivated; 
 sending a PDU session deactivation request message to each identified SMF; and 
 receiving, from each identified SMF, a respective PDU session deactivation response Acknowledgement message.

An Access and Mobility Function (AMF) comprising:
 at least one processor;   a non-transitory computer readable storage medium including software instructions configured to control the at least one processor to perform steps of:
 identifying Session Management Functions (SMFs) serving a set of one or more PDU sessions to be deactivated; 
 sending a PDU session deactivation request message to each identified SMF; 
 receiving, from each identified SMF, a respective PDU session deactivation response Acknowledgement message; and 
 responsive to receipt of the respective Release Notification Acknowledgement message from all of the identified SMFs, sending a Release Request message to an Access Network (AN).

